<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53559" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρφος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any
				small dry body</i>, esp. <i>dry stalk</i>, as of the <i>dry
				sticks</i> of cinnamon, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.111
			</span></i>; of <i>rice-straw</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				4.3.32
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				33
			</span></i>: generally, in pl., <i>dry twigs, chips, straws, bits of
				wool</i>, such as birds make their nests of, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				643
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
				32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				612b23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				10.14
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): collectivelyin sg., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				560b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.187c
			</span></i>: in sg., <i>chip</i> of wood, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				249
			</span></i>; <i>toothpick</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.22
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κινοῦσα μηδὲ κ</span>.
			'not stirring an inch', <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				474
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.67
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲ κ. ἐβλάβη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					980.9
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Philae</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ
				τῆς κύλικος κάρφος τῷ μικρῷ δακτύλῳ
			ἀφαιρετεῖν</span> Ion Hist.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			= Lat. <i>festuca</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.550b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>a small piece of wood</i> on which the watchword was written,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.36.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in pl.,
				<i>ripe fruit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				230
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				491
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				893
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				941
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆλις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.102
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάρφος</span> is
			v.l. (perh.right) in A.l.c., Plb.l.c.: perh. cogn. with
			Engl. <i>sharp.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
